pw basis for Al metal with ks_solver ppcg (projection preconditioned conjugate-gradient), multi k

SCF accuracy and reference validation (2026-10-14)
------------------------------------------------
This case checks energy, force, stress, symmetry, and the irreducible k-point
count. The previous scf_thr=1e-6 reciprocal-space criterion stopped after four
SCF steps, before stress was stable. Its totalstressref was 1108.971264 kbar;
the integrated PPCG implementation produced 1108.968411, exceeding the
unchanged 0.001 kbar acceptance tolerance by a deviation of 0.002853.
Tighter independent calculations instead approach 1107.675822 kbar.
The old reference and failure are retained in git history and this record.

The revised input explicitly selects scf_thr_type=2, the existing real-space
density criterion, with scf_thr=1e-10 and pw_diag_nmax=200. For this nonmagnetic
case the SCF quantity is integral(abs(rho_out-rho_in))/nelec. The two criterion
types have different definitions and units; their numeric thresholds are not
directly comparable. This selection also changes the existing charge-mixing
path to real space. It does not change the Hamiltonian, basis, occupations,
PPCG stopping criterion, or any global default.

Simply reducing the reciprocal-space threshold drove the automatic inner
tolerance close to double-precision roundoff: PPCG reported residuals around
2e-14 above its effective tolerance, and some CG/Davidson diagnostic runs
aborted during orthogonalization. Those runs were not used as references.
The real-space runs below converged without such failures; PPCG emitted no
inner-convergence warnings. The 200-step budget covers the initial PPCG solve.

Reference cross-check on d993c7a19, GNU 12.3, OpenMPI 4.1.2, Release CPU,
MPI/ELPA/Libxc enabled, LCAO/CUDA disabled, 4 ranks and one OpenMP/BLAS thread:

solver       real-space scf_thr   SCF steps   energy/eV             stress L1/kbar
PPCG         1e-10                14          -1882.177947234083     1107.6758226435
PPCG         1e-11                15          -1882.177947234496     1107.6758228259
CG           1e-9                 41          -1882.177947234288     1107.6759529017
Davidson     1e-10                26          -1882.177947233738     1107.6758361099
BPCG         1e-9                 13          -1882.177947234290     1107.6758167596

Stress L1 here is the sum of absolute tensor components from running_scf.log.
The property collector rounds individual components before summing: the
reference stores its PPCG result 1107.675822, not the higher-precision L1 above.
Compared with PPCG, CG and Davidson differ by less than 1.4e-4 and 1.4e-5 kbar
in the logged L1 stress, and less than 4e-10 eV in energy. Maximum individual
stress-component differences are below 4.4e-5 kbar. All forces are zero.
Tightening PPCG from 1e-10 to 1e-11 changes L1 stress by less than 2e-7 kbar.
PPCG at 1, 2, and 4 MPI ranks agrees within 6e-9 kbar, without inner warnings.
The saved b5d5fdb36 PPCG binary also agrees within 1e-8 kbar with the new input;
that older binary lacks Libxc, but this case uses the built-in PBE functional.
CG at 1e-10 did not reach SCF convergence within 50 or 100 steps, so neither
of those outputs is counted as a converged cross-check.

Only the input accuracy settings and numerical energy/stress references change.
The existing 1e-7 eV energy, 1e-4 eV/Angstrom force, and 1e-3 kbar stress
acceptance tolerances are unchanged. No local threshold override is added.
totaltimeref is historical metadata, not a new controlled performance result.

Run from tests/01_PW with an absolute path to the executable:
  OMP_NUM_THREADS=1 OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=1 MKL_NUM_THREADS=1 \
    bash ../integrate/Autotest.sh -a /path/to/abacus -n4 -o1 -j1 \
    -r '^819_PW_PPCG_Al$'

For independent checks, use fresh copies with the same structure, k mesh and
pseudopotential, change only ks_solver to cg/dav/bpcg and use the SCF thresholds
shown above. Check SCF completion and solver warnings as well as result.out;
an executable exit code or a final energy alone is not a convergence test.
The larger all-PPCG replacement suite and GPU runs are separate validations.
